# Vercel
.vercel

# Added by `vercel link`. The dotenv rules at the top of this file already
# cover .env files, including the `!.env.example` exception the CLI would
# otherwise undo by appending a blanket `.env*` after it.
.vercel

# Firecrawl onboarding doc. Carries a live API key in its last section, and
# lives at the repo root where "git add ." would sweep it in.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Bare `SKILL.md` matches at every
# depth, which silently swallowed every `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` — the one
# file a skill cannot be missing. A skill folder committed without it is a
# folder Claude Code ignores, and nothing in the diff would have said so.
/SKILL.md

# Eval results — transcripts and scores from a paid run, regenerated on demand.
# The harness is the artefact worth keeping; a results directory is one
# afternoon of it and would only make the diff noisy.
evals/results/

# Claude Code: the shared settings are committed; personal overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
